# OAuth2 discovery: a client derives the location of a well-known document from the URL the document is about
# and looks for it at the root of the host, because RFC 8414 and RFC 9728 insert the well-known segment in front
# of that URL's path. A web application deployed under a servlet context cannot answer there, so discovery stops
# after the first step unless the container redirects such a request into the context:
#
#   /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/clover           -> /clover/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
#   /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/clover/mcp/all/v1  -> /clover/mcp/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/all/v1
#
# The context is taken from the request, so no context name is written here. The authorization server metadata
# describe the issuer, which is the context itself; a Server deployed as the root application serves them where
# a client looks and needs no redirect for them. The protected resource documents describe the MCP endpoints,
# whose base has to be matched as the shortest prefix ending in /mcp: the deprecated /mcp alias of the main
# endpoint puts a second /mcp behind it, and taking the longer of the two would send a client to a path nothing
# serves. Only the two OAuth2 documents are matched — everything else under /.well-known/ is left alone, ACME
# challenges included.
#
# Read by the RewriteValve, declared on the Host in server.xml, which takes its rules from
# conf/<Engine>/<Host>/rewrite.config — conf/Catalina/localhost/rewrite.config in a default installation:
#
#   <Valve className="org.apache.catalina.valves.rewrite.RewriteValve" />
#
# Host level is where it has to sit: the request never reaches a context, so a context-level valve would not run.

RewriteRule ^/\.well-known/oauth-authorization-server(/.+)$ $1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server [R=302,L]
RewriteRule ^/\.well-known/oauth-protected-resource((?:/.+?)?/mcp)(/.+)$ $1/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource$2 [R=302,L]
RewriteRule ^/\.well-known/oauth-protected-resource((?:/.+?)?/mcp)$ $1/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource [R=302,L]
